  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will learn how to work with sequences and describe them recursively in an informal way. You will see how sequences are used to accomplish recurring tasks.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Give examples of a sequence.</item>
  <item> Explain the meaning of the term “sequence.”</item>
  <item> Explain the meaning of the term “term,” as it is used in a mathematical sequence.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are th <emphasis>ctivities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 4.14.1: Describe the Pattern</item>
  <item> 4.14.2: What Is a Sequence?</item>
  <list>
    <item> 4.14.2: Self Check</item>
    <item> 4.14.2: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>
  <item> 4.14.3: The Connection Between Sequences and Terms</item>
  <list>
    <item> 4.14.3: Self Check</item>
    <item> 4.14.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>
  <item> 4.14.4: Rules for a Sequence</item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item> 4.14.5: Practice</item>
  <item> 4.14.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
